---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
const entries = (await getCollection('produce')).sort((a, b) =>
  a.data.name.localeCompare(b.data.name),
);
---

<Layout title="About & sources">
  <div class="page-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">GOOD ADVICE HAS ROOTS</span>
    <h1>
      A little wiser.
      <br />
      <span>A little less waste.</span>
    </h1>
    <p>Friendly, practical guidance for the produce already in your kitchen.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="about-grid">
    <section class="info-card">
      <Icon name="leaf" size={28} />
      <h2>Freshness starts with a small habit.</h2>
      <p>
        Knowing where to put an avocado or when to wash berries can make everyday cooking a little
        easier. ProduceWise puts the useful answer first, then leaves room for curiosity.
      </p>
      <p>
        We’re starting with 10 fruits and vegetables. Each guide connects practical advice to its
        sources.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="info-card warm">
      <Icon name="book" size={28} />
      <h2>Clear sources. Clear limits.</h2>
      <p>
        Storage advice comes from university extension services, the FDA, USDA FSIS, and identified
        produce boards. Each guide lists what its sources support and when they were checked.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keeping times describe estimated quality, not guaranteed safety. Our initial source review
        is AI-assisted. It does not replace professional food-safety advice or product recalls.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="guide-section about-section">
    <h2>Nutrition you can trace.</h2>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/">USDA FoodData Central</a>, preferring Foundation
      Foods and using SR Legacy where it better matches the food. Each guide identifies the exact
      record, food form, and edible-portion basis. Values are typical estimates per 100 g, with
      sensible rounding.
    </p>
    <p>
      Missing data stays missing. We do not treat it as zero or quietly borrow it from another food.
      Nutrition updates are checked and saved separately from the website; browsing never needs a
      USDA account or API key.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-section about-section">
    <h2>Your guides, on your device.</h2>
    <p>
      Favorites stay in this browser’s local storage. We don’t require an account or send your saved
      list to a server. Saving a guide also attempts an offline download of the page, photo, and
      nutrition; a visible status tells you when it’s ready.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clearing browser data or running short on space can remove downloads. Saved guides can be
      refreshed from the saved page. Uncached pages and external source links need a connection.
    </p>
    <details class="source-details">
      <summary>
        Keep ProduceWise on your home screen <Icon name="chevron" size={16} />
      </summary>
      <p>
        On supported browsers, use “Install app” or “Add to Home Screen” from the browser menu. On
        iPhone or iPad, use Safari’s Share menu, then “Add to Home Screen.” Availability depends on
        your browser. Save the guides you want offline and check for “Ready offline” before
        disconnecting.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-section" id="image-credits">
    <span class="eyebrow">THE PEOPLE BEHIND THE PICTURES</span>
    <h2>Photography & credits.</h2>
    <p>
      Photos are hosted locally for fast loading and offline use. They have been resized and
      converted to WebP; CSS blends their backgrounds with the cards. Each adapted image retains its
      original license.
    </p>
    <div class="credits-grid">
      {entries.map((e) => (
        <div>
          <h3>{e.data.name}</h3>
          <p>
            <a href={e.data.image.source}>{e.data.image.author}</a>
          </p>
          <a href={e.data.image.licenseUrl}>{e.data.image.license} ↗</a>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p>
      For images licensed under GNU FDL 1.2, the{' '}
      <a href="/licenses/gfdl-1.2.txt">full license is included here</a>. USDA data is{' '}
      <a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-guide/">public domain (CC0)</a>. ProduceWise is
      independent and is not endorsed by these providers.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
